<section class="why-editableframe section" id="why-editableframe" aria-labelledby="why-heading">
  <div class="why-intro">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">WHY EDITABLEFRAME</span><h2 id="why-heading">A better fit for videos<br/><em>that keep evolving.</em></h2></div>
    <p>Generate a scene. Refine one detail. Try another direction.<br/>Choose EditableFrame when that creative back-and-forth is central to how you work.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="why-reasons">
    <article><span class="mono">01 / PRECISE CHANGES</span><h3>Each clip gets its own controls.</h3><p>A phone needs a model picker. A paper scene needs color and texture. Expose the details that matter, so a small change stays a small change.</p></article>
    <article><span class="mono">02 / ROOM TO EXPERIMENT</span><h3>People and agents share the edit path.</h3><p>Named scene details and validated commands give interfaces and AI tools a common way to make changes. Reversible history makes it easier to explore a direction and come back.</p></article>
    <article><span class="mono">03 / CREATIVE FREEDOM</span><h3>The controls can outlive the renderer.</h3><p>Canvas and Three.js power the studies here. New rendering libraries can connect through adapters while keeping the same approach to controls and edit history.</p></article>
  </div>
  <div class="why-context">
    <div><h3>Coming from Remotion or HyperFrames?</h3><p>Both are compelling ways to create video with code. Here’s where each approach starts.</p></div>
    <dl>
      <div><dt><a href="https://www.remotion.dev/docs/visual-editing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Remotion ↗</a></dt><dd>React compositions, with visual controls for composition props.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><a href="https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HyperFrames ↗</a></dt><dd>HTML, CSS and JavaScript video authoring, built for agents.</dd></div>
      <div class="why-our-focus"><dt>EditableFrame</dt><dd>A shared editing interface across scene renderers, with clip-specific controls and reversible commands at its core.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
  <div class="why-next"><p>Our emphasis is on keeping creative code easy to refine, as the scenes and the tools grow.</p><a class="text-link" href="#playground">Try a change for yourself ↑</a><a class="text-link why-scope" href="/guide/">Explore the beta scope ↗</a></div>
</section>
